{#description:
    This prompt is the initial prompt passed to slop-loop while it consumes a TODO file.
#}
{#defaults:
{
  "todo_file_path": "TODO.md",
  "plan_file_path": "PLAN.md",
  "notes_file_path": "NOTES.md",
  "todo_domain": "example-domain"
}
#}
@README.md
{% if include_context and todo_content %}

## TODO File: {{todo_file_path}}

{{todo_content}}
{% if plan_content %}
## PLAN File: {% if plan_file_path %}{{plan_file_path}}{% endif %}

{{plan_content}}
{% endif %}
Focus on the first incomplete section of the TODO file above.
{%- else %}

Read the first incomplete section of @{{todo_file_path}}.
{% if plan_file_path %}Detailed plan in @{{plan_file_path}}{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
Complete the tasks
Run ./scripts/spot-check to validate your changes
Mark the completed tasks in @{{todo_file_path}}
{% if notes_file_path %}Leave concise working notes in @{{notes_file_path}} as you go — record design decisions, gotchas, and anything a future reader would need.{% endif %}
Make note of any unrelated issues encountered for follow-up in TODO.followups.md
commit your changes with a descriptive message header:
{% if todo_domain %}
Include the TODO domain "{{todo_domain}}" in the commit scope alongside any crate names:

WRONG: "chore(repo-normalize): implement phase 5 changes"
CORRECT: "feat({{todo_domain}}, repo-normalize): filter by embeddings to detect duplicates"
{% else %}
WRONG: "chore(repo-normalize): implement phase 5 changes"
CORRECT: "feat(repo-normalize): filter by embeddings to detect duplicates"
{% endif %}
